adjudication.rationale:
In the diff, `getAuthorizationConditions()` sets `cachedAuthConditions` only after `await this.buildAuthorizationConditions()` resolves (same for filters):
```ts
if (this.cachedAuthConditions === undefined) {
  this.cachedAuthConditions = await this.buildAuthorizationConditions();
}
```
If `buildAuthorizationConditions()` throws (e.g., during DB issues while running `isOrgOwnerOrAdmin()` / org/team membership queries), the assignment never happens, leaving the cache `undefined` and causing every subsequent call to re-run the same query chain. This is a valid resiliency/operational concern (no negative caching/backoff), but it’s not a correctness defect per se.
